# Cancelling the cast must leave the game sound under CANTRIP_VERIFY (Game::goto once panicked here).
# Delighted Halfling's restricted mana ("spend this mana only to cast a legendary spell") is in Bot1's pool, so a Lightning Bolt
# cannot be paid with it; Bot1 names the Bolt's target, then cancels (CR 601.2, 733.1: an illegal or abandoned cast is undone as if
# it never happened). The game goes on: the Bolt is still in hand and the pool still holds the mana until the step ends.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Delighted Halfling
Lightning Bolt
Mountain
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Delighted Halfling.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Delighted Halfling.Activate(Color: Black; Ability: any color)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Cancel

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Mana = {B} (LegendarySpells, CantBeCountered)
Step = Main1
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 20
